import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Lemmas

/-!
# Weighted homogeneity under substitution and evaluation

Give the variable `i` the weight `w i`, and substitute for it a polynomial that is weighted
homogeneous of weight `w i` for weights `v` on the target variables. A weighted homogeneous
polynomial of weight `m` then becomes weighted homogeneous of weight `m` for the weights `v`. The
homogeneous case is `v = 1`: substituting polynomials homogeneous of degree `w i` turns a weighted
homogeneous polynomial of weight `m` into a homogeneous polynomial of degree `m`. In this case,
when the substitution is injective, the converse holds: a polynomial whose substitution is
homogeneous of degree `m` is itself weighted homogeneous of weight `m`.

The motivating substitution sends the variable `i` of `MvPolynomial (Fin n) R` to the elementary
symmetric polynomial `eᵢ₊₁`, which is homogeneous of degree `i + 1`
(`MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_esymm`). By the fundamental theorem of symmetric polynomials it is
injective, so the expression of a homogeneous symmetric polynomial in the elementary symmetric
polynomials is weighted homogeneous for the weights `i + 1`. The coefficients of a product
`∏ (X - C Ψ)` of linear factors with homogeneous constant terms of a common degree `m` supply
such symmetric polynomials (`MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_coeff_prod_X_sub_C`).

More generally, evaluating a weighted homogeneous polynomial of weight `m` at elements of the
graded pieces of weights `w i` of any graded algebra lands in its graded piece of weight `m`.
Conversely, the weighted homogeneous components of a polynomial over `R` are read off from the
substitution `X i ↦ X i * T ^ w i` into polynomials in an auxiliary variable `T`: the coefficient
of `T ^ n` is the component of weight `n`. This detects homogeneity of an ideal from its stability
under such substitutions, as for the ideal of relations of the Lazard ring. Specialising `T` to an
element `t` with pairwise distinct powers multiplies the coefficient of each monomial by `t` to the
power of its weight, so a polynomial that this substitution multiplies by `t ^ n` is weighted
homogeneous of weight `n`. Conversely, scaling the coordinates `x i` of a point by `c ^ w i`
scales the value of a polynomial of weight `n` by `c ^ n`.

Evaluating at a point is the substitution of constants. A weighted homogeneous polynomial of
nonzero weight vanishes wherever its variables of nonzero weight vanish, and the value of one of
weight zero (for canonically ordered weights) ignores the variables of nonzero weight. With the
indicator weight of a block `b` of variables `X_{b,l}`, so that weighted homogeneity is
homogeneity in block `b`: a polynomial that does not vanish at a point with zero block `b` has
degree zero in block `b`, and the blocks of degree zero can be replaced simultaneously by
arbitrary vectors without changing the value.

A polynomial algebra presentation also transports the weighted grading to its target: the
images of the homogeneous pieces form an internal graded algebra. A ring map from an integral
polynomial algebra with this grading preserves degrees exactly when the images of its variables
have the prescribed degrees, allowing additive regrading of the target.

Over a semiring without zero divisors, the lowest weighted homogeneous components of two
polynomials multiply to a nonzero component of their product. So, for weights in `ℝ≥0∞`, the
least weight of a monomial of a product is the sum of the least weights for the factors.

For canonically ordered weights with truncated subtraction, the weighted homogeneous component of
weight `n` of a product `p * q` with `q` weighted homogeneous of weight `d` is the component of
weight `n - d` of `p` times `q` when `d ≤ n`, and zero otherwise. This splits an element of an
ideal generated by weighted homogeneous elements into multiples of the generators of matching
weight.
A binomial `X^u - X^v` whose exponents have the same weight is weighted homogeneous of that
weight.

## Main results

* `MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.eval₂_mem`, `MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.aeval_mem`:
  evaluation at elements of graded pieces of the weights of the variables preserves weighted
  homogeneity.
* `MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.aeval`: substituting polynomials that are weighted
  homogeneous of the weights of the variables preserves weighted homogeneity.
* `MvPolynomial.weightedHomogeneousComponent_aeval`: such a substitution commutes with taking
  weighted homogeneous components.
* `MvPolynomial.isWeightedHomogeneous_of_isHomogeneous_aeval`: the converse of the homogeneous
  case, for an injective substitution.
* `MvPolynomial.isWeightedHomogeneous_of_aeval_C_pow_mul_X_eq`: a polynomial that the
  substitution `X i ↦ t ^ w i • X i` multiplies by `t ^ n` is weighted homogeneous of weight `n`,
  when the powers of `t` are pairwise distinct.
* `MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.aeval_pow_mul`: multiplying each coordinate `x i` by
  `c ^ w i` multiplies the value of a polynomial of weight `m` by `c ^ m`.
* `MvPolynomial.coeff_aeval_C_X_mul_X_pow`: the coefficient of `T ^ n` in the substitution
  `X i ↦ X i * T ^ w i` is the weighted homogeneous component of weight `n`.
* `MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.eval₂_eq_zero`: a polynomial of nonzero weight vanishes at
  a point whose coordinates of nonzero weight vanish.
* `MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.eq_zero_of_eval₂_ne_zero`: the block form, a nonzero value
  at a point with zero block `b` forces degree zero in block `b`.
* `MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.eval₂_congr`: the value of a polynomial of weight zero only
  depends on the coordinates of weight zero.
* `MvPolynomial.eval₂_congr_of_block_isWeightedHomogeneous_zero`: the block form, replacing all
  blocks of degree zero simultaneously preserves the value.
* `MvPolynomial.iInf_support_weight_mul`: without zero divisors, the least `ℝ≥0∞`-weight of a
  monomial of a product is the sum of the least weights for the factors.
* `MvPolynomial.IsWeightedHomogeneous.weightedHomogeneousComponent_mul_right`: the weighted
  homogeneous components of a product with a weighted homogeneous factor.
* `MvPolynomial.isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial_sub_monomial`: a binomial `X^u - X^v` with
  exponents of equal weight is weighted homogeneous.

## References

* J.-H. Evertse, *An improvement of the quantitative subspace theorem*, Compositio Math. 101
  (1996), §7, Lemma 26, for the block forms.
-/

public section

namespace MvPolynomial

variable {σ τ R : Type*}

section CommSemiring

variable [CommSemiring R]

/-- Evaluating a polynomial that is weighted homogeneous of weight `m`, along a ring homomorphism
`f` with values in the graded piece `𝒜 0` of a graded ring, at elements `g i` of the graded pieces
`𝒜 (w i)` gives an element of `𝒜 m`. -/
theorem IsWeightedHomogeneous.eval₂_mem {M A S : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] [CommSemiring A]
    [SetLike S A] [AddSubmonoidClass S A] {𝒜 : M → S} [SetLike.GradedMonoid 𝒜] {w : σ → M}
    {φ : MvPolynomial σ R} {m : M} (hφ : φ.IsWeightedHomogeneous w m) {f : R →+* A}
    (hf : ∀ r, f r ∈ 𝒜 0) {g : σ → A} (hg : ∀ i, g i ∈ 𝒜 (w i)) :
    eval₂ f g φ ∈ 𝒜 m := by
  induction hφ using IsWeightedHomogeneous.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | add p q _ _ ihp ihq => simpa using add_mem ihp ihq
  | monomial d r hr =>
    -- Write the weight of `d` as `0 + ∑ i, d i • w i`, matching the product of `f r ∈ 𝒜 0` with
    -- `∏ i, g i ^ d i ∈ 𝒜 (∑ i, d i • w i)`.
    rw [eval₂_monomial, ← hr, Finsupp.weight_apply, Finsupp.sum, ← zero_add (∑ _ ∈ _, _)]
    exact SetLike.mul_mem_graded (hf r) (SetLike.prod_pow_mem_graded 𝒜 w g d fun i _ ↦ hg i)

/-- Evaluating a polynomial that is weighted homogeneous of weight `m` at elements `g i` of the
graded pieces `𝒜 (w i)` of a graded algebra gives an element of `𝒜 m`. -/
theorem IsWeightedHomogeneous.aeval_mem {M A S : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] [CommSemiring A]
    [Algebra R A] [SetLike S A] [AddSubmonoidClass S A] [SMulMemClass S R A] {𝒜 : M → S}
    [SetLike.GradedMonoid 𝒜] {w : σ → M} {φ : MvPolynomial σ R} {m : M}
    (hφ : φ.IsWeightedHomogeneous w m) {g : σ → A} (hg : ∀ i, g i ∈ 𝒜 (w i)) :
    MvPolynomial.aeval g φ ∈ 𝒜 m := by
  rw [aeval_def]
  refine hφ.eval₂_mem (fun r ↦ ?_) hg
  rw [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]
  exact SMulMemClass.smul_mem r SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem

/-- Substituting, for each variable `i`, a polynomial that is weighted homogeneous of weight
`w i` for the weights `v` into a polynomial that is weighted homogeneous of weight `m` for the
weights `w` gives a polynomial that is weighted homogeneous of weight `m` for the weights `v`. -/
theorem IsWeightedHomogeneous.aeval {M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] {w : σ → M} {v : τ → M}
    {φ : MvPolynomial σ R} {m : M} (hφ : φ.IsWeightedHomogeneous w m) {g : σ → MvPolynomial τ R}
    (hg : ∀ i, (g i).IsWeightedHomogeneous v (w i)) :
    (MvPolynomial.aeval g φ).IsWeightedHomogeneous v m :=
  have := WeightedHomogeneousSubmodule.gradedMonoid (R := R) (w := v)
  hφ.aeval_mem (𝒜 := weightedHomogeneousSubmodule R v) hg

/-- Substituting, for each variable `i`, a polynomial that is weighted homogeneous of weight
`w i` for the weights `v` commutes with taking weighted homogeneous components: the component of
weight `m` of the substitution is the substitution of the component of weight `m`. -/
theorem weightedHomogeneousComponent_aeval {M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] {w : σ → M}
    {v : τ → M} {g : σ → MvPolynomial τ R} (hg : ∀ i, (g i).IsWeightedHomogeneous v (w i))
    (φ : MvPolynomial σ R) (m : M) :
    weightedHomogeneousComponent v m (MvPolynomial.aeval g φ) =
      MvPolynomial.aeval g (weightedHomogeneousComponent w m φ) := by
  classical
  induction φ using MvPolynomial.induction_on' with
  | monomial d r =>
    have hd := isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial w d r rfl
    rw [weightedHomogeneousComponent_of_mem (hd.aeval hg), weightedHomogeneousComponent_of_mem hd]
    split_ifs <;> simp
  | add p q hp hq => simp only [map_add, hp, hq]

/-- **Weighted homogeneous components as coefficients.** Substituting `X i * T ^ w i` for each
variable `X i` turns a polynomial into a polynomial in `T` whose coefficient of `Tⁿ` is its
weighted homogeneous component of weight `n`. -/
theorem coeff_aeval_C_X_mul_X_pow (w : σ → ℕ) (φ : MvPolynomial σ R) (n : ℕ) :
    (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun i ↦ Polynomial.C (X i) * Polynomial.X ^ w i) φ).coeff n =
      weightedHomogeneousComponent w n φ := by
  classical
  induction φ using MvPolynomial.induction_on' with
  | monomial d r =>
    -- Each factor `(X i * T ^ w i) ^ d i` contributes `T ^ (d i * w i)`.
    have h : MvPolynomial.aeval (fun i ↦ Polynomial.C (X i) * Polynomial.X ^ w i) (monomial d r) =
        Polynomial.C (monomial d r) * Polynomial.X ^ Finsupp.weight w d := by
      rw [aeval_monomial, monomial_eq]
      simp only [Finsupp.prod, Finsupp.weight_apply, Finsupp.sum, mul_pow, Finset.prod_mul_distrib,
        ← pow_mul', Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum, map_mul, map_prod, map_pow,
        Polynomial.algebraMap_apply, algebraMap_eq, smul_eq_mul]
      ring
    rw [h, Polynomial.coeff_C_mul_X_pow, weightedHomogeneousComponent_of_mem
      (isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial w d r rfl)]
  | add p q hp hq => simp [hp, hq]

/-- Substituting `t ^ w i • X i` for each variable `X i` multiplies the coefficient of every
monomial by `t` to the power of its weight. -/
theorem coeff_aeval_C_pow_mul_X (t : R) (w : σ → ℕ) (φ : MvPolynomial σ R) (d : σ →₀ ℕ) :
    (aeval (fun i ↦ C (t ^ w i) * X i) φ).coeff d = t ^ Finsupp.weight w d * φ.coeff d := by
  classical
  induction φ using MvPolynomial.induction_on' with
  | monomial e r =>
    have h : aeval (fun i ↦ C (t ^ w i) * X i) (monomial e r) =
        monomial e (t ^ Finsupp.weight w e * r) := by
      rw [aeval_monomial, monomial_eq]
      simp only [Finsupp.prod, Finsupp.weight_apply, Finsupp.sum, mul_pow, Finset.prod_mul_distrib,
        ← pow_mul', Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum, ← map_pow, ← map_prod, algebraMap_eq, smul_eq_mul,
        map_mul]
      ring
    rw [h, coeff_monomial, coeff_monomial]
    split_ifs with he
    · rw [he]
    · rw [mul_zero]
  | add p q hp hq =>
    simp only [map_add, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_add, Finsupp.coe_add, Pi.add_apply]
    rw [hp, hq, mul_add]

/-- **Weighted homogeneity from scaling.** If the powers of `t` are pairwise distinct and
substituting `t ^ w i • X i` for each variable `X i` multiplies `φ` by `t ^ n`, then `φ` is
weighted homogeneous of weight `n`. -/
theorem isWeightedHomogeneous_of_aeval_C_pow_mul_X_eq [IsCancelMulZero R] {t : R}
    (ht : Function.Injective (t ^ · : ℕ → R)) {w : σ → ℕ} {φ : MvPolynomial σ R} {n : ℕ}
    (h : aeval (fun i ↦ C (t ^ w i) * X i) φ = C (t ^ n) * φ) :
    φ.IsWeightedHomogeneous w n := fun d hd ↦ by
  have hd' := congrArg (fun p ↦ p.coeff d) h
  rw [coeff_aeval_C_pow_mul_X, coeff_C_mul] at hd'
  exact ht (mul_right_cancel₀ hd hd')

/-- **Weighted homogeneity from homogeneity of a substitution.** If `g i` is homogeneous of
degree `w i` for every variable `i` and substitution of the `g i` is injective, then a polynomial
whose substitution is homogeneous of degree `m` is weighted homogeneous of weight `m`. -/
theorem isWeightedHomogeneous_of_isHomogeneous_aeval {w : σ → ℕ} {g : σ → MvPolynomial τ R}
    (hg : ∀ i, (g i).IsHomogeneous (w i)) (hinj : Function.Injective (aeval (R := R) g))
    {φ : MvPolynomial σ R} {m : ℕ} (h : (aeval g φ).IsHomogeneous m) :
    φ.IsWeightedHomogeneous w m := by
  -- The degree-`m` part of the substitution of `φ` is the substitution of its weight-`m`
  -- component.
  have key : aeval g φ = aeval g (weightedHomogeneousComponent w m φ) :=
    (homogeneousComponent_eq_self h).symm.trans (weightedHomogeneousComponent_aeval hg φ m)
  rw [hinj key]
  exact weightedHomogeneousComponent_isWeightedHomogeneous m φ

/-- **Weighted homogeneity under scaling.** Multiplying each coordinate `x i` by `c ^ w i`
multiplies the value of a polynomial that is weighted homogeneous of weight `m` by `c ^ m`. -/
theorem IsWeightedHomogeneous.aeval_pow_mul {A : Type*} [CommSemiring A] [Algebra R A]
    {w : σ → ℕ} {φ : MvPolynomial σ R} {m : ℕ} (hφ : φ.IsWeightedHomogeneous w m) (c : A)
    (x : σ → A) :
    MvPolynomial.aeval (fun i ↦ c ^ w i * x i) φ = c ^ m * MvPolynomial.aeval x φ := by
  induction hφ using IsWeightedHomogeneous.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | add p q _ _ ihp ihq => rw [map_add, map_add, ihp, ihq, mul_add]
  | monomial d r hr =>
    -- Each factor `(c ^ w i * x i) ^ d i` contributes `c ^ (d i * w i)`.
    rw [aeval_monomial, aeval_monomial, ← hr]
    simp only [Finsupp.prod, Finsupp.weight_apply, Finsupp.sum, mul_pow, Finset.prod_mul_distrib,
      ← pow_mul', Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum, smul_eq_mul]
    ring

section Eval

variable {S M : Type*} [CommSemiring S] [AddCommMonoid M] {w : σ → M} {φ : MvPolynomial σ R}

/-- A weighted homogeneous polynomial of nonzero weight vanishes at every point whose
coordinates of nonzero weight vanish: each of its monomials involves a variable of nonzero
weight. -/
theorem IsWeightedHomogeneous.eval₂_eq_zero {m : M} (hφ : φ.IsWeightedHomogeneous w m)
    (hm : m ≠ 0) (f : R →+* S) {g : σ → S} (hg : ∀ i, w i ≠ 0 → g i = 0) :
    eval₂ f g φ = 0 := by
  refine eval₂Hom_eq_zero f g φ fun c hc ↦ ?_
  -- The monomial `X^c` has weight `m ≠ 0`, so it involves a variable of nonzero weight.
  obtain ⟨i, hi, hwi⟩ : ∃ i ∈ c.support, w i ≠ 0 := by
    by_contra! h
    refine hm ?_
    rw [← hφ hc, Finsupp.weight_apply, Finsupp.sum]
    exact Finset.sum_eq_zero fun i hi ↦ by rw [h i hi, smul_zero]
  exact ⟨i, hi, hg i hwi⟩

/-- If `F` is homogeneous of degree `d` in the variables `X_{b,l}` of block `b` and does not
vanish at a point whose block-`b` coordinates all vanish, then `d = 0`. -/
theorem IsWeightedHomogeneous.eq_zero_of_eval₂_ne_zero {ι κ : Type*} [DecidableEq ι]
    {F : MvPolynomial (ι × κ) R} {b : ι} {d : ℕ}
    (hF : F.IsWeightedHomogeneous (fun p : ι × κ ↦ if p.1 = b then 1 else 0) d) (f : R →+* S)
    {g : ι × κ → S} (hg : ∀ l, g (b, l) = 0) (h : eval₂ f g F ≠ 0) : d = 0 := by
  by_contra hd
  refine h (hF.eval₂_eq_zero hd f fun p hp ↦ ?_)
  obtain ⟨i, l⟩ := p
  obtain rfl : i = b := by simpa using hp
  exact hg l

variable [PartialOrder M] [IsOrderedAddMonoid M] [CanonicallyOrderedAdd M]

/-- Only variables of weight zero occur in a weighted homogeneous polynomial of weight zero, for
canonically ordered weights. -/
theorem IsWeightedHomogeneous.apply_eq_zero_of_coeff_ne_zero (hφ : φ.IsWeightedHomogeneous w 0)
    {c : σ →₀ ℕ} (hc : φ.coeff c ≠ 0) {i : σ} (hi : c i ≠ 0) : w i = 0 :=
  nonpos_iff_eq_zero.mp (hφ hc ▸ Finsupp.le_weight_of_ne_zero' w hi)

/-- The value of a weighted homogeneous polynomial of weight zero only depends on the
coordinates of weight zero, for canonically ordered weights. -/
theorem IsWeightedHomogeneous.eval₂_congr (hφ : φ.IsWeightedHomogeneous w 0) (f : R →+* S)
    {g₁ g₂ : σ → S} (h : ∀ i, w i = 0 → g₁ i = g₂ i) : eval₂ f g₁ φ = eval₂ f g₂ φ :=
  MvPolynomial.eval₂_congr _ _ _ fun hi hc ↦
    h _ (hφ.apply_eq_zero_of_coeff_ne_zero hc (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hi))

end Eval

/-- If `F` is homogeneous of degree `0` in each block `b ∈ Z` of variables `X_{b,l}`, its value
does not change when the coordinates of all the blocks in `Z` are replaced simultaneously by
arbitrary values. -/
theorem eval₂_congr_of_block_isWeightedHomogeneous_zero {S ι κ : Type*} [CommSemiring S]
    [DecidableEq ι] {F : MvPolynomial (ι × κ) R} {Z : Set ι}
    (hF : ∀ b ∈ Z, F.IsWeightedHomogeneous (fun p : ι × κ ↦ if p.1 = b then 1 else 0) 0)
    (f : R →+* S) {g₁ g₂ : ι × κ → S} (h : ∀ p : ι × κ, p.1 ∉ Z → g₁ p = g₂ p) :
    eval₂ f g₁ F = eval₂ f g₂ F :=
  MvPolynomial.eval₂_congr _ _ _ fun {p} {_} hi hc ↦ h p fun hp ↦ by
    simpa using (hF p.1 hp).apply_eq_zero_of_coeff_ne_zero hc (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hi)

section SupportWeight

open scoped ENNReal

variable [NoZeroDivisors R]

/-- Over a semiring without zero divisors, the least weight of a monomial in the support of a
product is the sum of the least weights in the supports of the factors. The weights take values
in `ℝ≥0∞`, so zero and infinite weights are allowed, and the infimum over the empty support of
`0` is `⊤`. -/
theorem iInf_support_weight_mul (w : σ → ℝ≥0∞) (P Q : MvPolynomial σ R) :
    ⨅ n ∈ (P * Q).support, n.weight w =
      (⨅ n ∈ P.support, n.weight w) + ⨅ n ∈ Q.support, n.weight w := by
  classical
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (le_iInf₂ fun n hn ↦ ?_)
  · by_cases hP : P = 0
    · simp [hP]
    by_cases hQ : Q = 0
    · simp [hQ]
    obtain ⟨d, hd, hdmin⟩ :=
      P.support.exists_min_image (fun n ↦ n.weight w) (support_nonempty.mpr hP)
    obtain ⟨e, he, hemin⟩ :=
      Q.support.exists_min_image (fun n ↦ n.weight w) (support_nonempty.mpr hQ)
    rw [le_antisymm (iInf₂_le d hd) (le_iInf₂ hdmin), le_antisymm (iInf₂_le e he) (le_iInf₂ hemin)]
    by_cases hp : d.weight w = ⊤
    · simp [hp]
    by_cases hq : e.weight w = ⊤
    · simp [hq]
    -- The product of the lowest weighted homogeneous components of `P` and `Q` is nonzero, and
    -- it is the weighted homogeneous component of `P * Q` of weight `d.weight w + e.weight w`.
    set P₀ := weightedHomogeneousComponent w (d.weight w) P
    set Q₀ := weightedHomogeneousComponent w (e.weight w) Q
    have hP₀ : P₀.coeff d ≠ 0 := by
      simpa [P₀, coeff_weightedHomogeneousComponent] using hd
    have hQ₀ : Q₀.coeff e ≠ 0 := by
      simpa [Q₀, coeff_weightedHomogeneousComponent] using he
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := ne_zero_iff.mp
      (mul_ne_zero (ne_zero_iff.mpr ⟨d, hP₀⟩) (ne_zero_iff.mpr ⟨e, hQ₀⟩))
    have hwg : g.weight w = d.weight w + e.weight w :=
      ((weightedHomogeneousComponent_isWeightedHomogeneous _ _).mul
        (weightedHomogeneousComponent_isWeightedHomogeneous _ _)) hg
    have hcoeff : (P₀ * Q₀).coeff g = (P * Q).coeff g := by
      rw [coeff_mul, coeff_mul]
      refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x hx ↦ ?_
      simp only [P₀, Q₀, coeff_weightedHomogeneousComponent]
      by_cases h0 : P.coeff x.1 * Q.coeff x.2 = 0
      · split_ifs <;> simp [h0]
      have h₁ : d.weight w ≤ x.1.weight w := hdmin _ (mem_support_iff.mpr (left_ne_zero_of_mul h0))
      have h₂ : e.weight w ≤ x.2.weight w :=
        hemin _ (mem_support_iff.mpr (right_ne_zero_of_mul h0))
      have hsum : x.1.weight w + x.2.weight w = d.weight w + e.weight w := by
        rw [← map_add, Finset.mem_antidiagonal.mp hx, hwg]
      have e₁ : x.1.weight w = d.weight w :=
        (ENNReal.le_of_add_le_add_right hq (hsum ▸ add_le_add le_rfl h₂)).antisymm h₁
      have e₂ : x.2.weight w = e.weight w :=
        (ENNReal.le_of_add_le_add_left hp (hsum ▸ add_le_add h₁ le_rfl)).antisymm h₂
      simp [e₁, e₂]
    rw [← hwg]
    exact iInf₂_le g (mem_support_iff.mpr (hcoeff ▸ hg))
  · rw [mem_support_iff, coeff_mul] at hn
    obtain ⟨x, hx, hne⟩ := Finset.exists_ne_zero_of_sum_ne_zero hn
    rw [← Finset.mem_antidiagonal.mp hx, map_add]
    exact add_le_add (iInf₂_le _ (mem_support_iff.mpr (left_ne_zero_of_mul hne)))
      (iInf₂_le _ (mem_support_iff.mpr (right_ne_zero_of_mul hne)))

end SupportWeight

section Component

variable {M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] [PartialOrder M] [CanonicallyOrderedAdd M] [Sub M]
  [OrderedSub M] [AddLeftReflectLE M] {w : σ → M}

attribute [local instance] weightedGradedAlgebra in
/-- The weighted homogeneous component of weight `n` of a product `p * q` with `q` weighted
homogeneous of weight `d` is the product of the component of weight `n - d` of `p` with `q` when
`d ≤ n`, and zero otherwise, for canonically ordered weights. -/
theorem IsWeightedHomogeneous.weightedHomogeneousComponent_mul_right
    {p q : MvPolynomial σ R} {d : M} (hq : q.IsWeightedHomogeneous w d) (n : M)
    [Decidable (d ≤ n)] :
    weightedHomogeneousComponent w n (p * q) =
      if d ≤ n then weightedHomogeneousComponent w (n - d) p * q else 0 := by
  classical
  rw [← weightedDecomposition.decompose'_apply, ← weightedDecomposition.decompose'_apply,
    DirectSum.Decomposition.decompose'_eq]
  exact DirectSum.coe_decompose_mul_of_right_mem _ n hq

end Component

end CommSemiring

/-- A binomial `X^u - X^v` with `∑ i, u i • w i = ∑ i, v i • w i` is weighted homogeneous of
weight `∑ i, u i • w i`. -/
theorem isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial_sub_monomial [CommRing R] {M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M]
    {w : σ → M} {u v : σ →₀ ℕ}
    (h : Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ w u = Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ w v) :
    IsWeightedHomogeneous w (monomial u (1 : R) - monomial v 1)
      (Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ w u) :=
  (isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial _ _ _ (Finsupp.weight_eq_linearCombination _ _)).sub
    (isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial _ _ _ ((Finsupp.weight_eq_linearCombination _ _).trans h.symm))

namespace WeightedHomogeneousSubmodule

/-- Transporting the weighted polynomial pieces along an algebra equivalence preserves the
multiplicative grading. -/
theorem gradedMonoid_map {M A : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] [CommSemiring R]
    [Semiring A] [Algebra R A] (w : σ → M) (e : MvPolynomial σ R ≃ₐ[R] A) :
    SetLike.GradedMonoid (fun n ↦ (weightedHomogeneousSubmodule R w n).map e.toLinearMap) where
  one_mem := Submodule.mem_map.mpr ⟨1, isWeightedHomogeneous_one R w, map_one e⟩
  mul_mem _ _ _ _ ha hb := by
    obtain ⟨a, ha', rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_map.mp ha
    obtain ⟨b, hb', rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_map.mp hb
    exact Submodule.mem_map.mpr ⟨a * b, ha'.mul hb', map_mul e _ _⟩

/-- An algebra equivalence transports the weighted polynomial decomposition to an internal
direct sum decomposition of its target. -/
theorem isInternal_map {M A : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] [DecidableEq M] [CommRing R]
    [Ring A] [Algebra R A] (w : σ → M) (e : MvPolynomial σ R ≃ₐ[R] A) :
    DirectSum.IsInternal (fun n ↦ (weightedHomogeneousSubmodule R w n).map e.toLinearMap) := by
  classical
  let := MvPolynomial.weightedGradedAlgebra (R := R) (w := w)
  have hW := DirectSum.Decomposition.isInternal (weightedHomogeneousSubmodule R w)
  apply DirectSum.isInternal_submodule_of_iSupIndep_of_iSup_eq_top
  · exact e.toLinearMap.iSupIndep_map e.injective hW.submodule_iSupIndep
  · rw [← Submodule.map_iSup, hW.submodule_iSup_eq_top, Submodule.map_top,
      LinearMap.range_eq_top]
    exact e.surjective

/-- A ring map from integral polynomials preserves regraded weights exactly when the images
of its variables have the given degrees. The target pieces may be additive subgroups rather
than submodules. -/
theorem map_mem_iff {M A S ι : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] [CommRing A]
    [SetLike S A] [AddSubgroupClass S A] [AddCommMonoid ι]
    (w : σ → M) (𝒜 : ι → S) [SetLike.GradedMonoid 𝒜] (r : M →+ ι)
    (f : MvPolynomial σ ℤ →+* A) :
    (∀ ⦃n⦄ ⦃p⦄, p.IsWeightedHomogeneous w n → f p ∈ 𝒜 (r n)) ↔
      ∀ i, f (X i) ∈ 𝒜 (r (w i)) := by
  refine ⟨fun h i ↦ h (isWeightedHomogeneous_X _ _ _), ?_⟩
  intro h n p hp
  have := AddSubgroupClass.zsmulMemClass (S := S) (M := A)
  have hpr : p.IsWeightedHomogeneous (r ∘ w) (r n) := fun d hd ↦ by
    simp only [← hp hd, Finsupp.weight_apply, map_finsuppSum, map_nsmul, Function.comp_apply]
  have hp' := hpr.aeval_mem (𝒜 := 𝒜) h
  have he : f.toIntAlgHom p = aeval (f.toIntAlgHom ∘ X) p :=
    DFunLike.congr_fun (aeval_unique f.toIntAlgHom) p
  simp only [Function.comp_def, RingHom.toIntAlgHom_apply] at he
  rw [he]
  exact hp'

end WeightedHomogeneousSubmodule

end MvPolynomial
